================================================================================
CLEAN-ROOM POSITION (read this before contributing any asset)
================================================================================

This repository is a CLEAN-ROOM implementation. It redistributes NO assets from the
Duckietown project and NO assets derived from them.

Specifically, and as a hard rule enforced by `scripts/check_clean_room.py` in CI:

  1. No mesh, material or scene file originating from `gym-duckietown`, `duckietown-world`,
     `dt-core` or any other Duckietown repository is present, in any form, converted or not.
     The Duckietown asset licenses are non-commercial and grant no redistribution right,
     so those files can never enter an Apache-2.0 repository.

  2. All robot geometry is authored from primitives (boxes, cylinders, spheres, capsules) in a
     hand-written URDF. All city geometry is generated at build time from a parametric
     generator into text USD (`.usda`). Binary and opaque geometry container formats
     (.obj, .glb, .gltf, .mtl, .stl, .dae, .fbx, .usd, .usdc, .usdz) are banned repository-wide.

  3. All road-marking textures are generated procedurally with PIL and numpy from the
     generator scripts in this repository. No texture is copied from any third party.

  4. What IS used from public Duckietown documentation is DIMENSIONAL FACT: tile pitch,
     lane width, tape widths and dash patterns, robot wheel radius and baseline, camera
     placement, encoder resolution and the published control conventions. Measurements and
     dimensions are facts and are not protected by copyright. They are cited, with their
     provenance class, in the specification and in `docs/architecture.md`.

  5. The gym-duckietown simulator, if used at all, is used ONLY as a locally installed
     third-party referee for one optional evaluation condition (C7). It is never vendored,
     never redistributed and never a dependency of this package.

Duckietown is a trademark of its respective owners. This project is not affiliated with,
endorsed by, or sponsored by the Duckietown Foundation. The name appears here solely to
describe interoperability and provenance of published dimensional facts.

================================================================================
THIRD-PARTY MATERIAL
================================================================================

The following third-party material may be vendored under `assets/`. Each item is listed in
`assets/MANIFEST.yaml` with its source and license, and the clean-room gate fails the build
if an unlisted binary asset appears.

  * AprilTag 36h11 marker images
      Source : https://github.com/AprilRobotics/apriltag-imgs
      License: BSD 2-Clause
      Use    : upscaled with NEAREST sampling onto sign cards. In this project the tags are
               VISUAL DISTRACTORS ONLY: at the trained observation resolution a 65 mm tag
               subtends 2 to 4 pixels and is not decodable. Nothing in the pipeline detects
               or decodes AprilTags.

  * HDRI environment maps (background imagery for the dome light)
      Source : CC0 sources only (for example Poly Haven, https://polyhaven.com)
      License: CC0 1.0 Universal (public domain dedication)
      Use    : background imagery and tint only, capped at six 2K files for the VRAM budget.
               HDRI files are gitignored; a fetch script records the exact URLs and sha256.

Full license texts for the above are reproduced in THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md.

